  "findings": [
    "Both hosts: inactive non-255 primary success removes the occupancy-byte load and zero test. It supplies capacity 20 to BZHIL after the 32-byte fingerprint compare. Secondary supplies 17. Mask clipping remains an emitted instruction; this is not a mask-free selector.",
    "Fingerprint 255 branches to occupancy-byte MOVZBL, TEST/JE, all-255 VPCMPEQB and BZHIL bounded by actual occupancy. Both paths join the same suffix-checked value address and two-byte callback.",
    "Producer, primary seeded permutation and secondary seeded permutation each use MOVL $40 to EDX immediately before BZHIQ. The complete count definition removes the earlier checksum-to-partial-count edge in these inspected hit CFGs. HT_HASH_MASK=2 is matched.",
    "All four qualified hit CFGs have zero calls or unresolved branches. Primary and secondary successes directly form a value address and MOVZWL both bytes into the scalar checksum ADD; the found count then contributes one. No callback/result-buffer boundary is introduced.",
    "Count mode tests occupancy before calculating the fingerprint; inactive calculates fingerprint before the 255 split and scans initialized fingerprint bytes for non-255 even on an empty bucket. Miss/empty work therefore also changes; no timing cost is assigned.",
    "Inactive duplicates candidate-walk blocks for non-255 and 255 fallback. Candidate TZCNT/BTR, suffix check, payload addressing and scalar reduction retain the same purpose, while hash scheduling and register allocation differ. Static whole-CFG size is not dynamic work per hit."
  ],
  "limits": [
    "Only these K40/W2 RefA10 arm1 independent-hit CFGs and host profiles are reviewed; no serial/aged/MM/other-geometry inference.",
    "No cycle/resource/cache causality, throughput claim or adoption recommendation.",
    "Complete-CFG instruction inventory includes mutually exclusive paths and timed setup; it is not a retired instruction count per operation.",
    "Original archived assembly and re-emitted ELF audit assembly hashes are distinct; exact address/opcode correspondence of every selected CFG instruction is separately checked below."
  ],
